id: 1
event: user
data: {"session_id":"1c047b6c-cb6b-4b06-9d0b-e14ca5330d2d","seq":1,"kind":"user","payload":{"text":"Work in your workspace and do all four steps:\n1. Research: use web_search and then web_fetch on a good source to find out what HTTP status code 418 means and which RFC defined it. Note the source URLs.\n2. Build a small web app in /workspace/app: index.html plus app.js, an 'HTTP status lookup' page with a text input and a button; typing a code (at least 10 common codes, including 418) shows its name and a one-line meaning. Serve it in the background with: cd /workspace/app && nohup python3 -m http.server 8000 >/tmp/server.log 2>&1 &\n3. Test it with the browser tool: open http://localhost:8000, type 418 into the input, click the button, check the page shows \"I'm a teapot\", and take a screenshot.\n4. Write a short report at /workspace/report.md (findings with source URLs, what you built, the test result) and convert it to /workspace/report.pdf with convert_file.\nReply with the paths of the PDF and the screenshot."},"at":1793932222462}

